# Project Overview

DisCompress is a browser-based video compression tool specifically designed for Discord file size limits. It allows users to compress videos to fit Discord's file size restrictions without leaving their browser.

## Key Files

- [index.html](mdc:index.html): Main entry point and UI for the application
- [compression.js](mdc:compression.js): Core functionality for video compression
- [styles.css](mdc:styles.css): Styling for the application

## Features

- Compress videos to fit Discord's file size limits (10MB, 50MB, 500MB)
- Adjustable quality settings to prioritize quality or size
- Custom target size options
- Real-time compression progress
- Before/after size comparison
- Drag-and-drop file upload

## Technical Details

DisCompress uses browser technologies:
- Canvas API to capture video frames
- MediaRecorder API to encode compressed video
- WebM container format with VP9 video codec
- Web Audio API for audio tracks
- File API for file handling

All processing is done client-side to preserve privacy.
